1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Chime

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:10,000
優しい陽だまりにチャイムがディレイする

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:19,000
頬を撫でる風、息吹は深く鳴ってゆく

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,000
遠回りの涙、名前付けた明日

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,000
重なる未来のノーライン

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:58,980
See you next time.

7
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:28,980
See you next time.

8
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:58,980
See you next time.

9
00:01:58,980 --> 00:02:01,280
Well, it's just that it's cold today.

10
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:04,480
It reminds me it's almost New Year's, so...

11
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:05,900
Almost?

12
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:06,920
Mm-hmm.

13
00:02:07,140 --> 00:02:08,000
Yeah, it's close.

14
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:10,780
Um, it's still November, though.

15
00:02:11,140 --> 00:02:11,640
Hey!

16
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:14,300
There he is.

17
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:15,700
Ah, morning.

18
00:02:15,700 --> 00:02:19,440
It's real chilly today, ain't it?

19
00:02:19,540 --> 00:02:20,700
He's in his blazer.

20
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:22,860
Why do you sound so excited about that?

21
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:23,460
So refreshing.

22
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:25,240
I haven't seen it since spring.

23
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:25,880
Huh?

24
00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:26,040
Huh?

25
00:02:26,540 --> 00:02:27,120
Uh...

26
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:29,660
You noticed, huh?

27
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:30,860
This mess.

28
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:36,460
Oh, your hair!

29
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:38,520
So that wasn't it?

30
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:39,960
Oh, man.

31
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:43,600
Then I should have told you my bedhead was just a new hairstyle.

32
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:45,600
Oh, my hair!

33
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:46,140
Kaze Haya!

34
00:02:46,780 --> 00:02:47,380
Hey!

35
00:02:47,540 --> 00:02:49,880
Come here, I got something awesome to show you!

36
00:02:50,260 --> 00:02:50,780
Awesome?

37
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:54,780
Okay, see you around.

38
00:02:54,780 --> 00:02:58,040
He said it was his bedhead.

39
00:02:58,520 --> 00:02:59,480
How cute!

40
00:03:00,640 --> 00:03:01,160
That?

41
00:03:01,480 --> 00:03:02,940
It's the new Ogura flavor!

42
00:03:03,860 --> 00:03:05,940
The juice box version of Hayakuni Nishu!

43
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:09,940
When Kaze Haya is surrounded by everyone like this...

44
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:12,720
I love how happy he seems.

45
00:03:13,780 --> 00:03:14,340
Oh, yeah.

46
00:03:14,580 --> 00:03:15,940
I used to think...

47
00:03:17,220 --> 00:03:19,740
It's incredible how they gather around him.

48
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:23,400
I want to be more like that one day.

49
00:03:24,780 --> 00:03:28,360
You're turning red!

50
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:36,240
Just as the seasons change, over time, little by little, my feelings start to as well.

51
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,060
Oh, my gosh.

52
00:03:41,980 --> 00:03:43,440
This is getting so annoying.

53
00:03:45,940 --> 00:03:47,080
Your boyfriend?

54
00:03:48,300 --> 00:03:48,900
Yep.

55
00:03:49,500 --> 00:03:50,800
That same college student?

56
00:03:51,480 --> 00:03:51,920
Yeah.

57
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:58,500
Every single day and every single night, he's like,

58
00:03:58,860 --> 00:03:59,800
What are you doing?

59
00:04:00,180 --> 00:04:01,040
Who are you with?

60
00:04:01,340 --> 00:04:02,540
Let's meet up right now.

61
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:04,280
Why don't you reply right away?

62
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:06,060
But why can't you come out?

63
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:07,400
Are you with a guy?

64
00:04:08,180 --> 00:04:08,980
Like...

65
00:04:08,980 --> 00:04:13,900
I wake up in the morning, then I go to school, after that I'm in class with my friends all day!

66
00:04:14,220 --> 00:04:15,740
And at night, I'm just sleeping!

67
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:17,640
Yeah, that is true.

68
00:04:17,900 --> 00:04:21,400
But seriously, Yano-jin, why are you dating a guy like that?

69
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:23,200
He...

70
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:24,280
asked.

71
00:04:24,280 --> 00:04:29,160
I wonder why guys are like this.

72
00:04:29,660 --> 00:04:32,840
They act mature and grown up, but then they show their true colors.

73
00:04:34,540 --> 00:04:38,660
I used to think it was such a pain in the butt to hang out with girls, that they were catty.

74
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:40,460
But guys are so much worse.

75
00:04:40,880 --> 00:04:43,280
Oh, is that how it is?

76
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:44,020
No.

77
00:04:44,240 --> 00:04:46,700
This is just a really problematic example.

78
00:04:46,700 --> 00:04:51,600
You'd have to love someone a lot to be that invested.

79
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:57,200
Seems romantic relationships come in all sorts of farms.

80
00:04:57,500 --> 00:04:58,300
Oh, Ryo.

81
00:04:58,600 --> 00:04:58,740
Hmm?

82
00:04:59,460 --> 00:05:01,240
I'm coming over tonight, so be home.

83
00:05:01,660 --> 00:05:02,020
Sure.

84
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:04,620
Let me keep playing that one game from where I left off.

85
00:05:05,180 --> 00:05:06,300
Okay, but...

86
00:05:06,300 --> 00:05:08,300
Or, how about a fighting game?

87
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:09,580
Definitely not.

88
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:14,860
When Chizu and Sanada are together, their energies really match each other.

89
00:05:14,860 --> 00:05:18,620
My eyes are only for Chizuru.

90
00:05:20,280 --> 00:05:23,800
Yes, I can't think of two people who would be better together.

91
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:25,320
A perfect pair.

92
00:05:26,780 --> 00:05:28,840
But I wonder how she feels.

93
00:05:30,120 --> 00:05:34,200
If I had to guess, I think she probably...

94
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:35,160
likes him back.

95
00:05:37,560 --> 00:05:38,520
Oh, Pops.

96
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:39,080
Hi there.

97
00:05:39,740 --> 00:05:40,940
Yo, sup, Chizu?

98
00:05:42,060 --> 00:05:42,980
It's cold.

99
00:05:42,980 --> 00:05:45,160
Oh, I'll help during winter break again.

100
00:05:45,420 --> 00:05:45,660
Okay?

101
00:05:46,020 --> 00:05:47,420
Uh, we appreciate it.

102
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:49,540
Good to have our poster girl around.

103
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:51,720
Yeah, I guess it is, isn't it?

104
00:05:52,020 --> 00:05:53,360
I'm gonna head upstairs now.

105
00:05:53,900 --> 00:05:54,360
Sure.

106
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:56,320
But I mean it when I say it, Chizu.

107
00:05:56,540 --> 00:05:58,740
I really do wish you were our daughter.

108
00:06:01,860 --> 00:06:04,200
If it were my choice, you know I would be.

109
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:12,480
Already going to bed?

110
00:06:12,840 --> 00:06:13,980
You took too long.

111
00:06:14,140 --> 00:06:14,740
What the hell?

112
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:15,900
I told you I was coming.

113
00:06:18,960 --> 00:06:19,480
Wait!

114
00:06:19,860 --> 00:06:21,580
Ah, dammit, I died!

115
00:06:22,680 --> 00:06:23,620
Stupid lion!

116
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:25,640
Chimera, you mean?

117
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:30,820
That reminds me of you talking in your sleep.

118
00:06:30,820 --> 00:06:31,820
Huh?

119
00:06:31,960 --> 00:06:34,080
I have never once talked in my sleep.

120
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:35,720
Little thing.

121
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:36,900
How dare.

122
00:06:37,380 --> 00:06:39,080
The dumb lion chimera.

123
00:06:43,380 --> 00:06:45,080
So, by the way...

124
00:06:45,080 --> 00:06:48,940
Is, um, there anything on your wish list, Rio?

125
00:06:49,380 --> 00:06:49,820
Hmm.

126
00:06:50,420 --> 00:06:51,540
Under 500 yen.

127
00:06:51,760 --> 00:06:53,040
A new baseball glove?

128
00:06:53,260 --> 00:06:54,280
500 yen!

129
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:57,620
Not shoulder massage tickets.

130
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:01,120
I'd be okay with anything.

131
00:07:01,920 --> 00:07:02,820
So, thank you.

132
00:07:03,540 --> 00:07:05,860
I never actually said I'm getting you something!

133
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:06,620
Sure.

134
00:07:06,980 --> 00:07:07,940
Thanks anyway.

135
00:07:09,340 --> 00:07:10,280
I'm leaving.

136
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:11,440
Okay.

137
00:07:15,060 --> 00:07:16,480
Oh, I meant to ask.

138
00:07:16,660 --> 00:07:17,280
On New Year's...

139
00:07:17,280 --> 00:07:24,540
Uh, actually, never mind.

140
00:07:24,900 --> 00:07:25,720
It's nothing.

141
00:07:26,200 --> 00:07:26,760
Good night!

142
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:32,380
I see.

143
00:07:34,140 --> 00:07:36,120
That's what you wanted to talk about.

144
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:43,600
Hello?

145
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:45,980
Yeah.

146
00:07:47,180 --> 00:07:48,700
Dad's taking a bath right now.

147
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:49,900
Sure.

148
00:07:51,380 --> 00:07:52,560
Wait, next week?

149
00:07:52,560 --> 00:08:05,920
I gotta tell her soon, huh?

150
00:08:10,260 --> 00:08:11,440
Sawako, Yono-chin!

151
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:13,280
Hey, shop with me today!

152
00:08:14,220 --> 00:08:14,700
Shopping!

153
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:16,580
Oh, no, I can't.

154
00:08:16,860 --> 00:08:17,180
Huh?

155
00:08:17,620 --> 00:08:18,100
Why?

156
00:08:18,500 --> 00:08:19,700
Because I'm meeting my boyfriend.

157
00:08:19,700 --> 00:08:22,160
And I need to see him as soon as possible.

158
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:24,280
Bye.

159
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:27,560
Uh, um...

160
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:28,640
Hmm?

161
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:29,920
I'm so afraid.

162
00:08:30,380 --> 00:08:30,900
Seriously?

163
00:08:31,360 --> 00:08:31,860
Awesome!

164
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:33,940
W-what are you buying?

165
00:08:34,460 --> 00:08:34,640
Hmm?

166
00:08:35,160 --> 00:08:36,680
Oh, uh...

167
00:08:36,680 --> 00:08:39,620
I'm getting Ryu a present for his birthday.

168
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:41,540
It's coming up soon.

169
00:08:42,660 --> 00:08:43,200
Oh!

170
00:08:44,680 --> 00:08:46,500
Yes, that's great!

171
00:08:46,680 --> 00:08:49,560
Well, you know, I'm like a crazy loyal friend, so...

172
00:08:50,360 --> 00:08:51,700
Let me go!

173
00:08:51,700 --> 00:08:52,700
Ow!

174
00:08:52,700 --> 00:08:53,700
Get out of here to chill, Joe!

175
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:54,700
You don't understand!

176
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:56,700
She's always looking at me with this passionate gaze!

177
00:08:56,700 --> 00:08:58,700
You're the one who's looking at her like that!

178
00:08:58,700 --> 00:09:01,700
You probably don't even know her name, do you?

179
00:09:03,700 --> 00:09:06,700
Hey, do you happen to believe in destiny?

180
00:09:06,700 --> 00:09:08,700
Listen, can't you hear it drawing near?

181
00:09:08,700 --> 00:09:11,700
The deafening sound of our combined fate's footsteps!

182
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:14,700
Yes, I've indeed come to return your feelings!

183
00:09:15,700 --> 00:09:16,700
Ew.

184
00:09:18,700 --> 00:09:19,700
Get up!

185
00:09:19,700 --> 00:09:20,700
Pull it together!

186
00:09:21,700 --> 00:09:23,700
You gotta stand up, Joe!

187
00:09:23,700 --> 00:09:24,700
No!

188
00:09:26,700 --> 00:09:28,700
What did you give him last year?

189
00:09:28,700 --> 00:09:30,700
Shoulder massage tickets, cause I was broke.

190
00:09:31,700 --> 00:09:32,700
Shoulder massage tickets?

191
00:09:33,700 --> 00:09:35,700
He chose to use them all up right there on the spot.

192
00:09:36,700 --> 00:09:38,700
Massaged his shoulders for three full hours.

193
00:09:38,700 --> 00:09:39,700
Wow!

194
00:09:39,700 --> 00:09:42,700
She must really care about Sonata's physical health, huh?

195
00:09:42,700 --> 00:09:44,700
This year, I've got a 500 yen budget.

196
00:09:44,700 --> 00:09:45,700
It's perfect!

197
00:09:54,700 --> 00:09:57,700
A new baseball glove is out of the question, but maybe a glove bag?

198
00:10:00,700 --> 00:10:01,700
Hold this for a sec.

199
00:10:08,700 --> 00:10:09,700
Yes!

200
00:10:09,700 --> 00:10:10,700
What now?

201
00:10:10,700 --> 00:10:11,700
I do have enough!

202
00:10:11,700 --> 00:10:12,700
Sweet!

203
00:10:12,700 --> 00:10:15,700
Then I guess I'll be extra generous this year!

204
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:18,700
Love!

205
00:10:23,700 --> 00:10:25,700
That was the perfect purchase!

206
00:10:25,700 --> 00:10:27,700
I'm really happy for you, Chizu!

207
00:10:35,700 --> 00:10:36,700
A mini skirt?

208
00:10:37,700 --> 00:10:41,700
Well, I thought it might be a good idea to change up my style once in a while.

209
00:10:42,700 --> 00:10:53,700
I want to ask.

210
00:10:54,700 --> 00:10:57,700
I wonder if it's okay to, or is it bad.

211
00:10:58,700 --> 00:10:59,700
But...

212
00:10:59,700 --> 00:11:03,700
If I go with my gut, right now seems like a good time.

213
00:11:03,700 --> 00:11:09,940
Um, Jisoo, I was wondering if you have a crush on someone.

214
00:11:11,540 --> 00:11:12,940
I did it!

215
00:11:16,760 --> 00:11:21,420
What the heck? That's so random. I do.

216
00:11:22,700 --> 00:11:25,000
It's always been a one-sided thing, though.

217
00:11:25,920 --> 00:11:26,560
Always?

218
00:11:28,740 --> 00:11:31,780
Yeah, I've had this little crush for a super long time.

219
00:11:31,780 --> 00:11:35,240
Wait, then. Does that mean...

220
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:37,840
We've been friends since childhood.

221
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:39,780
I knew it!

222
00:11:44,280 --> 00:11:48,880
The problem is, he really just thinks of me as a little sister.

223
00:11:49,240 --> 00:11:50,080
That's not true!

224
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:51,960
Huh? Say what?

225
00:11:52,480 --> 00:11:54,380
It's a... punch?

226
00:11:54,940 --> 00:11:58,100
It's fine, really. I'm okay with it.

227
00:11:58,100 --> 00:12:02,860
I'm a kid, after all. There's no way I'm even on his radar.

228
00:12:03,280 --> 00:12:04,640
I totally understand.

229
00:12:05,740 --> 00:12:09,180
That's why I've decided I'm gonna become a real catch.

230
00:12:09,740 --> 00:12:11,800
Once I grow up, you never know, right?

231
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:15,700
I'm glad I ended up asking her.

232
00:12:17,100 --> 00:12:21,040
I've never seen Jisoo with an expression like this before.

233
00:12:21,600 --> 00:12:25,860
But still, I don't get to see him much these days. I miss him.

234
00:12:26,480 --> 00:12:26,740
Huh?

235
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:30,440
He lives way up in Sapporo, so there's not much I can do about that.

236
00:12:30,680 --> 00:12:30,960
Oh.

237
00:12:31,660 --> 00:12:33,820
He didn't come back for last, Obon, either.

238
00:12:34,040 --> 00:12:35,940
Which means it's been almost a year now.

239
00:12:35,940 --> 00:12:39,120
But I know for sure he'll be coming back for New Year's.

240
00:12:39,460 --> 00:12:42,880
And he better watch out, because I'm a full-blown high school girl now.

241
00:12:43,420 --> 00:12:43,940
Wait.

242
00:12:44,520 --> 00:12:44,960
What?

243
00:12:45,900 --> 00:12:48,360
I'm getting kind of confused, so...

244
00:12:48,360 --> 00:12:50,640
Is it okay if I ask this straight out?

245
00:12:50,880 --> 00:12:51,380
What's up?

246
00:12:52,840 --> 00:12:55,340
So the person you've been talking about...

247
00:12:55,340 --> 00:12:57,000
You mean Sanada, right, Jisoo?

248
00:12:57,400 --> 00:12:57,720
Huh?

249
00:12:59,940 --> 00:13:01,040
Sawako, wait.

250
00:13:01,140 --> 00:13:02,940
Did you think I was talking about Ryu?

251
00:13:02,940 --> 00:13:04,220
Uh...

252
00:13:04,220 --> 00:13:04,760
Uh...

253
00:13:04,760 --> 00:13:05,180
Mm-hmm.

254
00:13:07,880 --> 00:13:09,440
You've got it all wrong.

255
00:13:10,220 --> 00:13:14,460
We've grown up together, so he's more like a brother than anything else.

256
00:13:14,980 --> 00:13:17,540
Though I wouldn't mind if we actually became siblings.

257
00:13:18,520 --> 00:13:20,820
You think of him as a brother?

258
00:13:24,340 --> 00:13:26,500
See, the person I like is...

259
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:27,480
His older brother.

260
00:13:28,480 --> 00:13:29,000
Huh?

261
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:29,440
Huh?

262
00:13:29,940 --> 00:13:30,400
Huh?

263
00:13:31,900 --> 00:13:32,840
Oh, man.

264
00:13:32,940 --> 00:13:34,700
Makes me blush.

265
00:13:37,100 --> 00:13:37,940
Um...

266
00:13:37,940 --> 00:13:38,380
Huh?

267
00:13:38,760 --> 00:13:39,940
Does Sanada...

268
00:13:40,620 --> 00:13:41,720
Know all of that?

269
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:42,380
Real?

270
00:13:42,920 --> 00:13:44,400
There's no way he wouldn't know.

271
00:13:45,980 --> 00:13:49,000
So this whole time, he already knew.

272
00:13:49,440 --> 00:13:49,920
Why?

273
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:50,940
Uh...

274
00:13:51,780 --> 00:13:51,940
Uh...

275
00:13:52,940 --> 00:13:53,740
No reason.

276
00:13:55,220 --> 00:13:56,860
Really, it's nothing.

277
00:13:57,720 --> 00:13:58,100
Huh?

278
00:13:59,040 --> 00:13:59,700
Second!

279
00:13:59,700 --> 00:14:04,040
Can't hear you, Sanada!

280
00:14:04,420 --> 00:14:04,820
Right!

281
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:06,560
You guys, too!

282
00:14:07,220 --> 00:14:07,660
Right!

283
00:14:08,160 --> 00:14:08,480
Again!

284
00:14:08,480 --> 00:14:08,800
Again!

285
00:14:11,760 --> 00:14:13,040
You hadn't gone home yet?

286
00:14:14,040 --> 00:14:16,380
Well, the gang and I were trying to cheer Joe up.

287
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:18,780
As reckless as usual, I see.

288
00:14:20,780 --> 00:14:24,140
But yeah, we decided we're gonna throw him a party to help him get back on his feet.

289
00:14:24,860 --> 00:14:25,760
Care to join us?

290
00:14:25,880 --> 00:14:26,900
We're thinking next weekend.

291
00:14:27,360 --> 00:14:28,100
Next weekend?

292
00:14:29,160 --> 00:14:32,100
Oh, that doesn't really work for me.

293
00:14:32,600 --> 00:14:32,860
Oh?

294
00:14:33,220 --> 00:14:33,960
You got plans?

295
00:14:34,460 --> 00:14:36,860
Not exactly, but...

296
00:14:36,860 --> 00:14:37,020
Hmm?

297
00:14:37,980 --> 00:14:39,480
That's when...

298
00:14:39,480 --> 00:14:40,680
My brother's back home.

299
00:14:40,680 --> 00:14:46,840
What about something like this?

300
00:14:47,240 --> 00:14:48,100
Looks cold.

301
00:14:48,860 --> 00:14:50,460
You'd really have to brace yourself.

302
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:51,460
I'd be shivering.

303
00:14:51,840 --> 00:14:54,040
That's no problem, because I'm all fired up!

304
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:55,100
Plus...

305
00:14:55,100 --> 00:14:56,640
Jesus is glowing right now.

306
00:14:57,300 --> 00:14:58,600
Would've made it in love.

307
00:14:59,500 --> 00:15:00,200
I get it.

308
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:03,600
Seeing the person you like can make you so incredibly happy.

309
00:15:04,420 --> 00:15:05,400
Oh, hey, Ryu.

310
00:15:05,600 --> 00:15:05,900
Morning.

311
00:15:06,720 --> 00:15:07,000
Night.

312
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:08,740
Good morning.

313
00:15:08,740 --> 00:15:09,780
Morning.

314
00:15:10,420 --> 00:15:10,620
Hmm?

315
00:15:13,020 --> 00:15:13,580
Morning.

316
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:15,560
Hey, what's up?

317
00:15:15,720 --> 00:15:17,160
Hi, good morning.

318
00:15:17,540 --> 00:15:19,760
Kasehaya, what do you think about these?

319
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:20,980
What's that?

320
00:15:21,260 --> 00:15:21,820
Winter stuff?

321
00:15:22,500 --> 00:15:24,040
Yep, a mini skirt.

322
00:15:24,880 --> 00:15:25,180
Huh.

323
00:15:25,720 --> 00:15:27,260
How much do those go for?

324
00:15:28,100 --> 00:15:30,620
Looks like 15,000 ye...

325
00:15:30,620 --> 00:15:33,920
I forgot I was dead broke right now.

326
00:15:35,160 --> 00:15:37,760
I really wanted to have it for New Year's.

327
00:15:37,760 --> 00:15:38,940
Oh, New Year's?

328
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:40,740
You don't get some cash then, right?

329
00:15:41,380 --> 00:15:43,040
No, that's too late.

330
00:15:43,460 --> 00:15:45,020
I don't know how long Toru's staying.

331
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:47,020
It may just be New Year's Eve or di-

332
00:15:47,020 --> 00:15:53,600
I, uh...

333
00:15:53,600 --> 00:15:55,720
So his name is Toru, huh?

334
00:15:57,040 --> 00:15:58,900
I didn't say anything just now.

335
00:15:59,540 --> 00:16:00,520
I didn't, right?

336
00:16:00,520 --> 00:16:03,440
Uh, yeah, I guess not.

337
00:16:05,100 --> 00:16:07,020
What's with all the drama, you guys?

338
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:09,000
Oh, Yanochi!

339
00:16:16,140 --> 00:16:17,300
We broke up.

340
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:19,180
So we dumped you?

341
00:16:19,180 --> 00:16:20,760
No, I dumped him!

342
00:16:21,680 --> 00:16:23,480
And it was a total nightmare.

343
00:16:24,180 --> 00:16:26,180
Yeah, can definitely see that.

344
00:16:26,500 --> 00:16:30,180
I was honest about how I felt and gently suggested breaking up, and he...

345
00:16:30,180 --> 00:16:41,000
Oh, I'm sorry.

346
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:42,340
I-I didn't mean to.

347
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:44,660
You're the only thing I have left, Yanochi.

348
00:16:45,940 --> 00:16:47,480
Let's move in together, okay?

349
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:48,480
Please?

350
00:16:48,700 --> 00:16:49,660
This is pointless.

351
00:16:50,220 --> 00:16:53,200
The guy isn't listening to a single word coming out of my mouth.

352
00:16:53,200 --> 00:16:56,580
But yeah, I didn't really like him.

353
00:16:57,320 --> 00:16:58,860
He was just totally annoying.

354
00:16:59,560 --> 00:17:00,300
Wow, sorry.

355
00:17:00,480 --> 00:17:01,860
I assumed you were into him.

356
00:17:02,380 --> 00:17:04,440
After all my complaining, that was your takeaway?

357
00:17:05,360 --> 00:17:08,340
I want to comfort her, but I can't think of the right words to say.

358
00:17:09,120 --> 00:17:10,760
I know that it wasn't meant to be.

359
00:17:11,940 --> 00:17:15,960
But at the same time, it's not any fun when things have to end like this, either.

360
00:17:16,800 --> 00:17:17,460
Poor thing!

361
00:17:18,900 --> 00:17:19,340
Huh?

362
00:17:19,940 --> 00:17:21,160
What's going on with you?

363
00:17:21,160 --> 00:17:23,360
Why are you acting like I was the one who got dumped?

364
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:25,320
There's someone else who got dumped here?

365
00:17:25,980 --> 00:17:27,200
Comrades and heartbreak!

366
00:17:27,720 --> 00:17:29,140
Don't lump me in with you!

367
00:17:29,440 --> 00:17:32,080
Any kind of romance involves some sort of heartbreak.

368
00:17:32,500 --> 00:17:34,560
But it's still tough each time.

369
00:17:36,480 --> 00:17:39,420
Like I said, I'm the one who did the breaking up, not him!

370
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:40,820
Hide your pain from me!

371
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:43,260
Come on, let's talk about it together!

372
00:17:43,260 --> 00:17:45,500
Let's be honest, or are you, Yano?

373
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:48,420
Ryu.

374
00:17:49,260 --> 00:17:49,440
Hmm?

375
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:53,800
You haven't told Yoshida yet, have you?

376
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:56,400
Well, it isn't easy to bring it up.

377
00:17:57,320 --> 00:18:00,040
Do you think you'd tell her, or...

378
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:01,280
Would I?

379
00:18:02,420 --> 00:18:02,820
Hmm.

380
00:18:03,760 --> 00:18:04,800
I think I would.

381
00:18:05,360 --> 00:18:07,180
And the rest, that's on her.

382
00:18:07,760 --> 00:18:08,780
That's not my call.

383
00:18:10,400 --> 00:18:10,700
Hmm.

384
00:18:10,700 --> 00:18:13,060
I figured you might say that, Shota.

385
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:13,980
Huh?

386
00:18:14,860 --> 00:18:17,500
Well, you're probably right, though.

387
00:18:18,220 --> 00:18:23,840
Because if Chizuru doesn't know, and we end up running into my brother, it's gonna be a real problem.

388
00:18:24,720 --> 00:18:25,040
Hmm.

389
00:18:26,340 --> 00:18:28,520
But still, it's hard.

390
00:18:28,520 --> 00:18:30,980
New Year's?

391
00:18:30,980 --> 00:18:31,980
A mini skirt?

392
00:18:31,980 --> 00:18:33,480
Sounds great to me.

393
00:18:33,480 --> 00:18:34,140
Really?

394
00:18:34,140 --> 00:18:34,640
Good.

395
00:18:34,640 --> 00:18:36,400
I'm thinking about getting a frilly one.

396
00:18:36,400 --> 00:18:38,560
Uh, get one that looks good on you.

397
00:18:38,900 --> 00:18:40,520
Uh, you think it'd look bad?

398
00:18:41,280 --> 00:18:42,880
This is real girl talk.

399
00:18:43,220 --> 00:18:44,600
I'm so curious.

400
00:18:44,980 --> 00:18:46,680
I wonder what kind of guy he is.

401
00:18:46,680 --> 00:18:51,100
Hey, can we go see him, too?

402
00:18:51,420 --> 00:18:51,740
What?

403
00:18:52,040 --> 00:18:52,380
No.

404
00:18:52,820 --> 00:18:53,920
I think I'd die.

405
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:56,300
Jesus seems so happy.

406
00:18:57,800 --> 00:18:58,540
Oh, no.

407
00:18:58,640 --> 00:19:00,440
I'm getting all excited about myself.

408
00:19:00,700 --> 00:19:02,360
Even though our Yano is suffering.

409
00:19:02,860 --> 00:19:03,600
I'm fine.

410
00:19:03,700 --> 00:19:05,220
You really don't have to worry about it.

411
00:19:05,380 --> 00:19:06,480
I'm so sorry, Yano.

412
00:19:06,560 --> 00:19:07,700
You have to cheer up.

413
00:19:08,100 --> 00:19:11,600
Hey, why don't we throw an awesome party to help get your spirits up?

414
00:19:11,680 --> 00:19:12,680
We can use my house.

415
00:19:13,320 --> 00:19:14,400
Uh, yeah, sure.

416
00:19:14,920 --> 00:19:16,560
Then let's have a sleepover on Friday.

417
00:19:16,900 --> 00:19:17,600
You too, Sawago.

418
00:19:19,180 --> 00:19:19,780
Sleepover?

419
00:19:20,340 --> 00:19:21,620
I can come, too?

420
00:19:22,100 --> 00:19:24,240
We're all going to play a fighting game together.

421
00:19:24,720 --> 00:19:25,780
Oh, a game?

422
00:19:28,860 --> 00:19:30,220
Chizuru, it's me.

423
00:19:30,660 --> 00:19:30,900
Huh?

424
00:19:31,780 --> 00:19:32,900
I'm coming in.

425
00:19:33,300 --> 00:19:33,740
Hey!

426
00:19:33,840 --> 00:19:34,080
Shh!

427
00:19:34,460 --> 00:19:36,560
Don't just barge in here without permission.

428
00:19:37,060 --> 00:19:38,940
I could have been changing clothes or something.

429
00:19:39,420 --> 00:19:40,180
Yeah, yeah.

430
00:19:40,580 --> 00:19:42,600
And I could say the exact same thing to you.

431
00:19:43,360 --> 00:19:44,060
What's up?

432
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:46,240
It's a rare treat for you to come visit me.

433
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:46,980
Here.

434
00:19:46,980 --> 00:19:47,000
Here.

435
00:19:48,140 --> 00:19:48,560
Hmm.

436
00:19:49,260 --> 00:19:50,460
You don't want any?

437
00:19:52,720 --> 00:19:53,260
Huh?

438
00:19:55,720 --> 00:19:56,540
We should talk.

439
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:04,860
Hmm?

440
00:20:04,860 --> 00:20:05,780
Hmm?

441
00:20:05,780 --> 00:20:11,220
What's wrong?

442
00:20:11,940 --> 00:20:12,780
It's nothing.

443
00:20:15,860 --> 00:20:17,900
Chizuru, here's the thing.

444
00:20:18,040 --> 00:20:18,580
No, go home!

445
00:20:19,300 --> 00:20:19,520
Hmm?

446
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:20,840
Just leave.

447
00:20:20,960 --> 00:20:21,560
Get out of here!

448
00:20:22,340 --> 00:20:24,840
No, but I need to talk.

449
00:20:24,840 --> 00:20:25,640
Ow!

450
00:20:25,640 --> 00:20:26,000
Ow!

451
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:39,960
What am I supposed to do?

452
00:20:43,460 --> 00:20:46,700
Up until now, just interacting with others

453
00:20:46,700 --> 00:20:48,720
was enough to overwhelm me.

454
00:20:49,200 --> 00:20:51,400
Because that alone was so difficult.

455
00:20:52,160 --> 00:20:54,160
I never even thought about romance.

456
00:20:54,960 --> 00:20:57,400
But I'm sure that romantic relationships

457
00:20:57,400 --> 00:21:00,060
must be just as difficult as friendship.

458
00:21:00,060 --> 00:21:05,820
The reason I can understand that, at least a little,

459
00:21:06,300 --> 00:21:08,800
is probably because of how certain I am

460
00:21:08,800 --> 00:21:11,320
that I've fallen in love with Kaze Haya.

461
00:21:11,320 --> 00:21:30,940
No way!

462
00:21:30,940 --> 00:21:37,820
わからないそれが答えなんだって

463
00:21:37,820 --> 00:21:42,180
シャボンタモ飛ばそう

464
00:21:42,340 --> 00:21:49,280
空まではきっと届かないうちに壊れそう

465
00:21:49,620 --> 00:21:55,040
噛んだで知りたいの永遠じゃない

466
00:21:55,220 --> 00:22:00,520
このま

467
00:22:00,520 --> 00:22:16,900
But I'll make it important to see only one plane.

468
00:22:16,900 --> 00:22:21,240
From here, I'll be able to find you as a lecture.

469
00:22:30,520 --> 00:22:34,440
Next time, dream.

470
00:23:00,520 --> 00:23:30,500
Next time, dream.

